              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "A, B, and C are the centres of circles of the same size"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.369,
            0.641,
            0.392
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Are Triangles Possible for any Lengths?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.401,
            0.848,
            0.458
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can one construct triangles having any given sidelengths? Are there lengths for which it is impossible to construct a triangle? Let us explore this."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.466,
            0.735,
            0.49
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Construct a triangle with sidelengths 3 cm, 4 cm, and 8 cm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.497,
            0.736,
            0.519
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is happening? Are you able to construct the triangle?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.526,
            0.846,
            0.568
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? Here is another set of lengths: 2 cm, 3 cm, and 6 cm. Check if a triangle is possible for these sidelengths."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.586,
            0.792,
            0.627
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? Try to find more sets of lengths for which a triangle construction is impossible. See if you can find any pattern in them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.808,
            0.583,
            0.896,
            0.636
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 12,
              "bbox": [
                0.808,
                0.583,
                0.896,
                0.636
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_5_image_12.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.636,
            0.848,
            0.712
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We see that a triangle is possible for some sets of lengths and not possible for others. How do we check if a triangle exists for a given set of lengths? One way is to actually try to construct the triangle and check if it is possible. Is there a more efficient way to check this?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.721,
            0.362,
            0.741
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Triangle Inequality"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.745,
            0.847,
            0.782
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider the lengths 10 cm, 15 cm and 30 cm. Does there exist a triangle having these as sidelengths?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.782,
            0.849,
            0.896
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To tackle this question, let us study a property of triangles. Imagine a small plot of plain land having a tent, a tree, and a pole. Imagine you are at the entrance of the tent and want to go to the tree. Which is the shorter path: (i) the straight-line path to the tree (the red path) or (ii) the straight-line path from the tent to the pole, followed by the straight-line path from the pole to the tree (the yellow path)?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.806,
            0.938,
            0.845,
            0.955
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "151"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 18,
